use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` despite its docstring.\n\nChange: switch `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nBranch updated with latest main; CI run ci-0002 passed on 0a9452f727.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-bankers-rounding-0a9452f727"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 746948, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_014twx1ZLSJbRgr7C6er76D1", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-bankers-rounding-0a9452f727", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 746948, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_014twx1ZLSJbRgr7C6er76D1", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 753946, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n**The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` was using round-half-up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`). Its own docstring says banker's rounding per FIN-212, and that's what `tests/test_money.py` checks for. So the test failed on 2.665, which should round to 2.66.\n\n**The fix:** On a new branch, `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding`, I switched it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That's the only change.\n\n**CI:** The first run passed, but the service wouldn't open the PR because the branch was behind main. I merged the latest main into the branch, confirmed the fix was still there, and ran CI again on the updated branch (run ci-0002). It passed, and then I opened the PR.\n\nI haven't merged it. Policy says merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason"