/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` despite its docstring.\n\nChange: switch `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-bankers-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The branch is behind main. I'll merge main into it, then run CI again on the new head before opening the PR.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01K59GdmTXmiaANnisizUCwZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding"}, "name": "update_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01TjrNbPvnArfo9vC9QNaEWy", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "ref": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_016xbUuQp84tmHhDB32VyXrv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fin-212-0a9452f727"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01SDtaYzcmQ9R5BBSH7rDcgS", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0002"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014twx1ZLSJbRgr7C6er76D1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` despite its docstring.\n\nChange: switch `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nBranch updated with latest main; CI run ci-0002 passed on 0a9452f727.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fin-212-bankers-rounding-0a9452f727"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n**The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` was using round-half-up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`). Its own docstring says banker's rounding per FIN-212, and that's what `tests/test_money.py` checks for. So the test failed on 2.665, which should round to 2.66.\n\n**The fix:** On a new branch, `fix/fin-212-bankers-rounding`, I switched it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That's the only change.\n\n**CI:** The first run passed, but the service wouldn't open the PR because the branch was behind main. I merged the latest main into the branch, confirmed the fix was still there, and ran CI again on the updated branch (run ci-0002). It passed, and then I opened the PR.\n\nI haven't merged it. Policy says merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}